					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1157018#post-2268154</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1157018/contingency#post-2268154</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 10 Apr 2015 22:36:34 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>1324229</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm ambivalent on this canon at the moment; some of the stuff has been quite interesting or at least well-executed enough to keep me going. However, the stuff that focuses mostly on the established author avatars is, quite frankly, boring. I've never found the &quot;Clef is 166's dad and cares for her very much&quot; angle compelling. Nor have I have found &quot;Clef is le master troll&quot; a particularly endearing or interesting quality. In fact, besides some of the goofier less OTT termination stuff, I don't really care for Clef as a character.</p> <p>The vast majority of this story is back-and-forth between a character I don't find interesting and a character that I primarily remember (I might be totally off-base with this, though) as his hyper-competent assistant that he likes to mess with. -1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
